 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # project_id is the id of the Scaleway project to discover Instances in (mandatory).
+  - project_id: "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key (token) to use for authentication (mandatory).
+    # It is sent as the X-Auth-Token HTTP header on every API request.
+    # See https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/console/account/how-to/generate-api-key/
+    secret_key: "..."
+
+    # api_url is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # api_url: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # zone is an optional Scaleway availability zone to discover Instances in.
+    # By default, fr-par-1 is used.
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # name_filter is an optional filter to limit the discovered Instances to those matching the given name.
+    #
+    # name_filter: "..."
+
+    # tags_filter is an optional list of tags to limit the discovered Instances to those having all the given tags.
+    #
+    # tags_filter: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Only running Instances are discovered. Each discovered target has an
+[`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<public_ip>:<port>`, where `<public_ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the Instance, or its private IPv4 address if the Instance has no
+public IP, while `<port>` is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the state of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the availability zone of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_region`: the region of the Instance, derived from its zone.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the id of the organization the Instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: the comma-separated list of tags of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_id`: the id of the security group of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_name`: the name of the security group of the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_id`: the id of the image used to boot the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_name`: the name of the image used to boot the Instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_arch`: the architecture of the image used to boot the Instance.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag, default: 30s.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
